 "title": "Ten-step struck tones (demo)",
 "demo": true,
 "contributors": [
  {
   "name": "the what3sounds project",
   "role": "wrote this demonstration"
  }
 ],
 "statement": "A demonstration written by Claude for this preview, and nobody's tradition. Forty-eight recordings of a synthesised struck bar, tuned to ten equal steps in each octave. It is here to show the samples renderer, which plays recordings as they are, and the other way of fitting a vocabulary to the grid: this codebook fixes the size of a place (about a hectare and a half on the hexagon grid, about half that on the pentagons) and lets its own smallness decide how many tones a place gets, which comes to a seven-note phrase.",
